# ==============================================================================
# ZPHS VADADA - POSTGRESQL & SUPABASE ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================
#
# To connect to your Supabase PostgreSQL instance:
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Run the SQL files from supabase/ in the Supabase SQL Editor:
#      - supabase/schema.sql
#      - supabase/policies.sql
#      - supabase/seed.sql
# 3. Copy your Project URL and Anon Public Key from Project Settings > API
# 4. Create a .env file in this directory with the following variables:

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-public-key

# Note: If these variables are not provided, the application runs with an
# offline-first persistent PostgreSQL local-store engine with full CMS capabilities
# so the application remains 100% operational in all environments.
